{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>So much as the tread of a foot.</b> Even the treading of the foot upon it — I do not give you permission except with their consent." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'Up to the tread of their foot' — until the day comes of the treading of the foot upon the Mount of Olives, as it is said (Zechariah 14): ״ועמדו רגליו ביום ההוא על הר הזיתים״. And elsewhere they interpreted: 'Up to the tread of a foot' — until (Isaiah 63): ״פורה דרכתי לבדי״." "<b>For it is an inheritance to Esav.</b> From Avraham: ten nations I gave to Avraham — seven that are yours, and Keni and Kenizi and Kadmoni, which are those of Ammon and Moav and Seir. I gave one of them to Esav and the two to the children of Lot."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:48.494035344Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}